# Agent/metadata probe paths -> real 404, NOT the app.
#
# The catch-all below exists so real routes like /defi-forge work on a single-page site.
# Its side effect was that ANY missing path returned 200 plus the full homepage, so an
# automated client asking "do you have an llms.txt?" was told yes and handed HTML.
# A missing file must answer 404. A failed check must never render as a clean result.
#
# Cloudflare Pages serves genuine static files before consulting this file, so real
# assets (robots.txt, sitemap.xml) are unaffected. These rules only catch what is absent.
# Listed explicitly rather than by wildcard: splat semantics for mid-path patterns like
# /*.json are not something this project has verified, and an over-broad rule here would
# break routing. Explicit and correct beats clever and unverified.
/llms.txt                 /404.html   404
/llms-full.txt            /404.html   404
/agents.json              /404.html   404
/agent.json               /404.html   404
/ucp.json                 /404.html   404
/acp.json                 /404.html   404
/openapi.json             /404.html   404
/mcp.json                 /404.html   404
/.well-known/*            /404.html   404

# Single-page app fallback — every real route is served by index.html.
/*    /index.html   200
